ते हैं। इसीलिए कहा गया है कि आखेटक को न तो मरना चाहिए न ही जीवित रहना\nचाहिए क्योंकि मरना तथा जीना दोनों ही उसके लिए कष्टकारक होते हैं। ये पशु आखेटक सामान्य",
      "textEn": "80\n\nTherefore, every seeker, liberated, and worker, including everyone, should benefit by chanting and listening to the glory of God. Although the sound of God's divine qualities is equally beneficial to everyone, but those who are liberated\nIt is especially dear to them. It is said in Shrimad Bhagwat (8.3.20) that pure devotees whose\nmaterial desires are exhausted and who take refuge in the lotus feet of God,\nby chanting and listening to the holy name of God, remain constantly immersed in the ocean of bliss. According to this verse, Narad and other residents of Shwetadvipa, such as devotees, are always seen chanting the name of the Lord.\nBecause by doing so, they remain delighted both in Brahmata and internally. The seekers who want to be liberated,\ndo not depend on the pleasures of the senses, but by chanting the name of the Lord, they remain engaged in meditation.\nThe workers want to do good deeds that please their ears and hearts,\nBut sometimes they also want to praise and listen to God, yet they do it in a direct form\nThey do not. But devotees always voluntarily listen to, sing, and remember the works of God.\nAnd in this way, they remain completely satisfied, even if these appear to be matters of sensory gratification. Parikshit Maharaj\nHe became free just by listening to the divine stories of the activities of God. Therefore, they were pleasing to the ears.\nThat is, they adopted the method of listening. All living beings should adopt this method. To separate these people devoid of divine bliss, Parikshit Maharaj has used the word 'virajyet puman'.\nHe has used words. The puman is indicative of any person, whether male or female, or between the two. Due to the egoistic intellect, we grieve, but a person devoid of egoistic intellect experiences joy in spiritual\nlistening and chanting.\nTherefore, a person engrossed in bodily consciousness, due to not being able to spiritual\nascend, certainly keeps killing himself. Such a person is called an animal slayer.\nIs. Those who are not interested in listening to and chanting the holy name of God, the hunters of animals,\nremain detached from spiritual life. Such hunters in this life and in the next life also\nalways remain sad. That is why it is said that the hunter should neither die nor live.\nBecause dying and living are both painful for him. These are common animal hunters"
